Each fiber forks one in which a writer writes a copy of a cell's contents, then calls a top-level function value whose body computes a function that masks or lends the fiber (an `if`, a `case`, a block, a pipe, a call's answer, `Maybe.withDefault`, inside a tuple, a `List.map` callback, a helper, a value of another module and its helper, a lend); no function hosts, accepted (ownership-v3-kernel.md §13 item 12, *A defect*, (d), *The ways in*, row 8; #2696). Its live twin is CellTopValueCallLive.
